<title>BRAZIL: Brazil court delays telecom ruling.</title>
<headline>Brazil court delays telecom ruling.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's highest court has postponed until Thursday a session to judge the constitutionality of a law laying out the framework for the deregulation of the telecommunications sector, a spokesman said.</p>
<p>The spokesman said the Supreme Federal Tribunal had more urgent matters to deal with, including a ruling on the extradition of a former Peruvian central bank president.</p>
<p>The court was due to rule on a claim by opposition parties that Brazil's basic legislation for the telecommunications sector is unconstitutional.  </p>
<p>The ruling could affect the upcoming auction of cellular telephone Band B concessions. Bids for 10 concession areas are due in by April 7.</p>
<p>((-- Adrian Dickson, Brasilia newsroom 55-61-2230358))</p>
</text>
